        <key>construction</key>
        <string>Retain the genuine same-cut designed small-cap letter body without resizing. Fit only the native middle-wave component horizontally to the actual body ink width plus visible native-wave-derived end clearance. Keep its vertical coordinates, amplitude and vertical stroke thickness unchanged, and centre it at half the actual SC frame. Preserve native body edge-spacing roles through one whole horizontal translation and a new advance. This is explicit optical width fitting of a fixed modifier, not a whole letter/capital reduction or ordinary unmodified SC alias.</string>
